<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Cait</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pictish province in the far north of mainland Scotland, whose name survives in Caithness and in Gaelic Cataibh for Sutherland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cait is one of the seven Pictish provinces named after the legendary sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cruithne-legendary-king">Cruithne</a>. The name, perhaps 'cat people', survives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caithness">Caithness</a>, the Norse 'headland of the Cats', and Gaelic Cataibh, the name for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutherland">Sutherland</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing reliable is known of its government or rulers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/broch">Broch</a> towers and later Pictish symbol stones show a long-settled farming and seafaring population in the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From the 9th century Norse settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caithness">Caithness</a>, which came under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-orkney">Earldom of Orkney</a>. The area was gradually brought into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland</a> in the 12th and 13th centuries.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion<